KG42.register("edges-1aa3a1a565e2bed8db6e2965",{"id":"S-ec6919fcb49a2d6f","source":"COMP-b3f649e90c1f17b9","type":"links","target":"COMP-fe1c33d7a61b4b97","evidence_class":"S","scientific_acceptance":false,"relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"paper_ids":["13-consensus_product_differentiation"],"assertions":[{"id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R004::E::v141-c-R004-E002","paper":"13-consensus_product_differentiation","rule_id":"v141-c-R004","rule_ref":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R004","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E002","source":"bidding.supply","target":"coordination.price_signal","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g02-e19"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C001"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-b3f649e90c1f17b9","target":"COMP-fe1c33d7a61b4b97","source_occurrence_id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R004::V::bidding.supply","target_occurrence_id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R004::V::coordination.price_signal","source_unit_id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::M01::bidding.supply","target_unit_id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::M01::coordination.price_signal","omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Consumer-side quantity feedback in decentralized MBED forward-market negotiation. | Consumer-side quantity submission for decentralized RCI negotiation. | Individually calculated price estimates for the same bilateral trade in the fully decentralized RCI implementation. | Information disclosure in the RCI implementation of MBED. | Per-iteration communication between neighboring agents in RCI negotiation. | Producer-side quantity feedback in decentralized MBED forward-market negotiation. | Producer-side quantity submission for decentralized RCI negotiation. | Termination of iterative RCI coordination.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g01-e31","v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g02-e20","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e22"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"02191423f8ddb40926d18e4d8d510f92a860602361b23fc4622a01e42c6de7f8","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"M01","source_definition":"Price-signal coordination supplies the perceived-price input to the inverse-gradient target power setpoint used in updating the producer's bilateral offered quantity. Scope: Producer quantity updates in the decentralized RCI implementation of MBED. Condition: Agent n operates as a producer during an RCI iteration. Updating the trading-price dual variables precedes updating the producer's bilateral offered quantities; power-boundary dual updates also occur before the quantity-update step. Scope: Within-iteration ordering of RCI updates for producers. Condition: Each RCI iteration containing the producer P-update. Different price offers lead the producer to try to concentrate its offered quantity with the neighboring agent having the most interesting price and offer nothing to the others; the source describes direct-solution outcomes as usually binary. Scope: The direct-solution approach discussed for MBED local subproblems. Condition: A producer's local subproblem is solved directly with different offered trade prices. Each bilateral offered quantity is constrained to be nonnegative. The producer P-update enforces this sign restriction through its max operator at each iteration. Scope: Producer bilateral supply quantities in MBED and their RCI updates. Condition: Agent n operates as a producer. The sum of a producer's bilateral offered quantities is subject to its lower and upper power-injection bounds. RCI enforces the power-boundary constraints through Lagrangian relaxation. Scope: Aggregate producer supply feasibility and RCI treatment of power boundaries. Condition: Producer quantities must satisfy the bounds at a feasible MBED solution; the RCI implementation treats these constraints through Lagrangian relaxation. A producer must send its current bilateral offered quantity to the corresponding neighboring agent as part of the prescribed quantity-and-price information bundle. Scope: Information exchanged by producers with their neighboring negotiating agents during RCI. Condition: At each RCI iteration.","target_definition":"The producer's current offered bilateral quantity enters the price-estimate update through the trading-reciprocity imbalance term. Scope: Producer-side quantity feedback in decentralized MBED forward-market negotiation. Condition: During an RCI price update involving a producer's bilateral quantity. The consumer's current requested bilateral quantity enters the price-estimate update through the trading-reciprocity imbalance term. Scope: Consumer-side quantity feedback in decentralized MBED forward-market negotiation. Condition: During an RCI price update involving a consumer's bilateral quantity. Performing the RCI updates requires sharing the producer's current offered bilateral quantity with its communication neighbor as part of the mandatory quantity-and-price message. Scope: Producer-side quantity submission for decentralized RCI negotiation. Condition: At each RCI iteration, for a producer and its communication neighbor. Performing the RCI updates requires sharing the consumer's current requested bilateral quantity with its communication neighbor as part of the mandatory quantity-and-price message. Scope: Consumer-side quantity submission for decentralized RCI negotiation. Condition: At each RCI iteration, for a consumer and its communication neighbor. Each agent must send its bilateral price estimate to its communication neighbor as part of the prescribed information exchange. Scope: Per-iteration communication between neighboring agents in RCI negotiation. Condition: At each RCI iteration. The participants' separately calculated price estimates for a given bilateral trade must agree, λ_nm = λ_mn. Scope: Individually calculated price estimates for the same bilateral trade in the fully decentralized RCI implementation. Condition: After convergence. Reaching optimality through RCI does not require sharing agents' internal production/consumption parameters or product-differentiation criterion parameters. Scope: Information disclosure in the RCI implementation of MBED. The iterative process stops when convergence is established; convergence criterion (26) is optional. Scope: Termination of iterative RCI coordination. Condition: When algorithmic convergence is established under the prescribed stopping criteria.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The producer's current offered bilateral quantity enters the price-estimate update through the trading-reciprocity imbalance term. Scope: Producer-side quantity feedback in decentralized MBED forward-market negotiation. Condition: During an RCI price update involving a producer's bilateral quantity.","expression":"λ_nm^{k+1} = λ_nm^k − β^k (λ_nm^k − λ_mn^k) − α^k (P_nm^k + P_mn^k) (11), for a producer n ∈ Ω_p with P_nm^k ≥ 0 (9d) and m ∈ ω_n; the term (P_nm^k + P_mn^k) is the trading-reciprocity imbalance (innovation) term that carries the producer's current offered bilateral quantity into the price-estimate update.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":["x-P-nm","x-P-mn","x-lambda-nm","x-lambda-mn"],"parameter_refs":["theta-alpha-k","theta-beta-k"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g02-e07"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e07","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p02-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":"995","section":"II-A. Peer-to-Peer Trading","anchor_text":"m- The power set-points of an agent n are constrained by the ny power boundaries Pn and Pn, ms a Pn ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The role of each agent is restrained to either producer or consumer (P_n P̄_n ≥ 0) as it simplifies the following derivations. Hence, the decision variables are constrained in sign depending on whether the agent n is a producer (P_nm ≥ 0) or a consumer (P_nm ≤ 0)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e24","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p05-c2r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":5,"printed_page":"998","section":"III-B. Dual Updates","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON POWER SYSTEMS, VOL. 34, NO. 2, MARCH 2019 equality constraint (as in the dual a","equation_id":"(11)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"This is referred to as the λ-update, λ_nm^{k+1} = λ_nm^k − β^k (λ_nm^k − λ_mn^k) − α^k (P_nm^k + P_mn^k) (11) where α^k and β^k are sequences of positive factors such that any excitation is persistent, so that the series of each sequence diverges [12]. The tuning of these parameters is key to the performance of the algorithm and will usually be a trade-off between convergence speed and resilience to change of setup. The tuning relies as much on the value of the parameters as on the ratio between the two. The performance could be improved by using adaptive factors that adjust this ratio."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e19","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p06-c1r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":6,"printed_page":"999","section":"III-D. Operational Aspects of the Iterative Process","anchor_text":"privacy and support data security since very little information is shared and only with those agents","equation_id":"(23)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Here to perform the RCI updates, a minimum set of informa-tion is to be shared. As such, at each iteration of the process, the set F nmk  of information sent by an agent n ∈Ω to a neighboring agent m ∈ωn at iteration k must be the following:\n             F nmk = {P nm,k   λknm}                (23)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e07","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p05-c2r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":5,"printed_page":"998","section":"III-B. Dual Updates","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON POWER SYSTEMS, VOL. 34, NO. 2, MARCH 2019 equality constraint (as in the dual a","equation_id":"(11)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"where αk and βk are sequences of positive factors such that any excitation is persistent, so that the series of each sequence diverges [12]. The tuning of these parameters is key to the performance of the algorithm and will usually be a trade-off between convergence speed and resilience to change of setup. The tuning relies as much on the value of the parameters as on the ratio between the two. The performance could be improved by using adaptive factors that adjust this ratio."}],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Consumer-side quantity feedback in decentralized MBED forward-market negotiation. | Consumer-side quantity submission for decentralized RCI negotiation. | Individually calculated price estimates for the same bilateral trade in the fully decentralized RCI implementation. | Information disclosure in the RCI implementation of MBED. | Per-iteration communication between neighboring agents in RCI negotiation. | Producer-side quantity feedback in decentralized MBED forward-market negotiation. | Producer-side quantity submission for decentralized RCI negotiation. | Termination of iterative RCI coordination.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g01-e31","v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g02-e20","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e22"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E002","source":"bidding.supply","target":"coordination.price_signal","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g02-e19"]},"paper_scope_note":"The λ update, P update, and required communication of RCI have direct formula basis; only protocol component dependencies are allowed, and the values of k and k+1 or the roles of consumer and producer are not conflated."}}],"assertion_ids":["13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R004::E::v141-c-R004-E002"]});
